      "message": "Host should be allowed to read calibration data, even if not updated: after reboot, it may want to re-ask the EC, even if the EC did not recalculate.\n\nWe should return an error when the EC asks for calibration information when the sensor does not support it.\n\n               Old AP                 |    New AP\n--------+-----------------------------+----------------------------------------\nNewer EC:  will not ask at boot,      | May ask for sensor not yet supported (MAG) at boot\n           not register MKBP handler  |  - return EC_RES_UNAVAILABLE: the AP will not\n           code not exercised.        |     register a listener.\n                                      |  - return some data otherwise, 0s is fine.\n--------+-----------------------------+---------------------------------------- \nOlder EC:      NA                     | EC_RES_INVALID_COMMAND",
